From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samu Kaarlela <samu@Samus-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:20:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Resolve EGL 1.5 client functions before a display exists

epoxy_conservative_egl_version() returns 14 when no display is current,
so EGL 1.5 core functions that are meant to be called before any display
exists can never be resolved. In particular eglGetPlatformDisplay()
aborts with:

  No provider of eglGetPlatformDisplay found.  Requires one of:
      EGL 15

even though the implementation (e.g. ANGLE) supports EGL 1.5, since
there is no display to query until eglGetPlatformDisplay() has
returned one.

EGL 1.5 allows querying the client library version with
eglQueryString(EGL_NO_DISPLAY, EGL_VERSION). Use it when no display is
current. Older implementations reject EGL_NO_DISPLAY there with
EGL_BAD_DISPLAY; clear that error and keep the previous assumption of
EGL 1.4.
---
 src/dispatch_egl.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dispatch_egl.c b/src/dispatch_egl.c
index 3f0c789..4a44c2b 100644
--- a/src/dispatch_egl.c
+++ b/src/dispatch_egl.c
@@ -31,11 +31,24 @@ int
 epoxy_conservative_egl_version(void)
 {
     EGLDisplay dpy = eglGetCurrentDisplay();
+    int client_version;
 
-    if (!dpy)
-        return 14;
+    if (dpy)
+        return epoxy_egl_version(dpy);
 
-    return epoxy_egl_version(dpy);
+    /*
+     * Without a current display, use the client library version. EGL 1.5
+     * supports eglQueryString(EGL_NO_DISPLAY, EGL_VERSION), which lets 1.5
+     * client entry points such as eglGetPlatformDisplay() resolve before any
+     * display exists. Earlier implementations fail with EGL_BAD_DISPLAY;
+     * clear that error and keep assuming 1.4.
+     */
+    client_version = epoxy_egl_version(EGL_NO_DISPLAY);
+    if (client_version)
+        return client_version;
+
+    (void)eglGetError();
+    return 14;
 }
 
